Given the following erroneous code, debug and update a MongoDB document.

```
const mongoose = require('mongoose'); 

// connection to MongoDB
mongoose.connect('mongodb://localhost/products', {useNewUrlParser: true, useUnifiedTopology: true});

// Defining Schema
let itemSchema = new mongoose.Schema({ 
    _id : mongoose.Schema.Types.ObjectId,
    description : String, 
});

// Compiling schema into a model
let itemModel = mongoose.model('items', itemSchema); 

// Updating a document
itemModel.findByIdAndUpdate({ _id: '5e9697d50a5173c078b5306b', description: 'This item is now available in 3 sizes'},  (err) => { 
    if (err)
        console.log(err); 
    else
        console.log("Update successful"); 
    mongoose.connection.close(); 
});
```

The information you need to apply is as follows:

Database name: products
Collection name: items
Document ID: 5e9697d50a5173c078b5306b
Field to update: description
Value: This item is now available in 3 sizes

Remember that you also need to handle any errors during the update and close the connection after the operation.
